The '''2021–22 Primera División RFEF ''' season was the first and the only season under the name [[Primera División RFEF]], the new third highest level in the [[Spanish football league system]]. It succeeded the old Segunda División B, which renamed itself [[Segunda División RFEF]] and downgraded to the fourth level in the pyramid.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.abc.es/deportes/futbol/abci-federacion-desvela-misterio-nueva-segunda-denominara-primera-division-rfef-202009141930_noticia.html |title=La Federación desvela el misterio: La nueva Segunda B se denominará Primera División RFEF |language=es |trans-title=The Federation reveals the mystery: The new Second B will be called First Division RFEF |date=15 September 2020 |first=Jorge |last=Abizanda |work=[[ABC (newspaper)|ABC (Spain)]]}}</ref> Forty teams participated, divided into two groups of twenty clubs each based on geographical proximity. In each group, the champions automatically promoted to [[Segunda División]] and the second to fifth placers played promotion play-offs and the bottom five were relegated to the Segunda División RFEF.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://as.com/futbol/2021/04/15/mas_futbol/1618483534_728171.html |work=AS |title=Así será el formato de la nueva Primera División RFEF |trans-title=This will be the format of the new Primera División RFEF |last=Arés |first=Ruby |date=15 April 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://rfef.es/noticias/luis-rubiales-reune-clubes-nueva-primera-rfef-es-momento-construir-algo-juntos|title=Luis Rubiales reúne a los clubes de la nueva Primera RFEF: 'Es el momento de construir algo juntos'|trans-title=Luis Rubiales brings together the new Primera RFEF's clubs: "It's time to build something together"|publisher=Royal Spanish Football Federation|language=es|date=15 April 2021}}</ref>

==Overview before the season==
A total of 40 teams joined the league, including four relegated from the [[2020–21 Segunda División]] and 36 promoted from the [[2020–21 Segunda División B]].

